      "tool_id": "hirearchy::services",
      "description": "The standing services you can request from your direct reports and the ones you offer, with contract and\n        playbook versions, inputs, budget per request and the record so far (requests, outcomes, runs, feedback).",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "tool_id": "hirearchy::blueprint_example",
      "description": "A ready-to-edit blueprint (YAML with a comment on every field and a one-paragraph schema summary).\n\n        kind: \"research\" (facts from the web with source URLs, fact-checked), \"documents\" (write from the user's local\n        files, no web; uses `needs.inputs`, read-only folders), \"code\" (software in a repo workspace, with tests and\n        local commits) or \"analysis\" (the user's data files, read-only, analysed by a checked script). Replace every\n        <PLACEHOLDER> with what the user told you (ask for what is missing; do not invent lists), delete what does not apply, then call propose_org with the text. Read-only.\n\n        service: true for work the user wants again and again (\"every week\", \"whenever I...\"): the template then offers it\n        as a standing service (`services:` with inputs, acceptance, deliverable and budget per request, and an optional\n        first request) instead of a one-off `task:`.\n        ",
      "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "kind": {
            "default": "research",
            "title": "Kind",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "service": {
            "default": false,
            "title": "Service",
            "type": "boolean"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ],
